    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Driven by seasonal conditions making travel more feasible, a measurable increase in border crossings occurred in March, with 8,268 people apprehended. Observers note that while enforcement measures have resulted in historically low crossing numbers year-to-date, the people seeking safety or opportunity now face the consequences of a system that prioritizes restriction over protection. The legislative stalemate on enforcement funding leaves vulnerable individuals in limbo, underscoring the human cost of political deadlock at the U.S. border.",
